name.description:
The session's display name. Required for `team-workspace` (e.g. "Sprint 1");
the same name in the same team while it runs is the same session. With `story`
it opens another session in the story's workspace under `<storyId>#<name>`;
without it the story's own session.

dryRun.description:
Check everything and report what would be created, writing nothing;
reports rendered argv for commands. Keep other defaults unless asked;
report `schedule_in_words`, the first `next_fires` and the `agent`.
Validation includes a bad `when`, under 5 minutes, the 25 enabled-routine
cap, no visible `agent`, an Only me agent for a team routine, or a taken `id`.

minGap.description:
Optional: the least time between two of its deliveries (`30m`, `2h`;
1m to `7d`). A fire inside it folds into the last one instead of
waking you again. Set it when each wake starts heavy work.

onClick.description:
Make the row actionable. `{type:"goto-agent",agentId}` jumps to the agent's
running terminal; `{type:"open-file",path}` opens the path in the viewer;
`{type:"show-message"}` (default) opens the conversation view.

